From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Loic Poulain <loic.poulain@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 17:42:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: connector: pcie-m2-e: Add vendor
 LGA connector compatible

Some modules (e.g. the Qualcomm QCA2066/QCNFA765) expose the same M.2
Key E interface signals but are physically soldered as an LGA package
rather than plugged into a real M.2 Key E connector socket. Such designs
are not actual M.2 Key E connectors, so describe them with a dedicated
vendor-specific compatible while keeping "pcie-m2-e-connector" as a
fallback for the shared signal semantics.

Add "qcom,pcie-m2-1418-lga-connector" for the M.2 LGA 1418 found on
Arduino Ventuno Q (Monaco Monza).

Add "qcom,pcie-m2-1620-lga-connector" for the M.2 LGA 1620 found on
The Lenovo Thinkpad T14s.

Reviewed-by: Krzysztof Kozlowski <krzysztof.kozlowski@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Manivannan Sadhasivam <mani@kernel.org>
Reviewed-by: Bartosz Golaszewski <bartosz.golaszewski@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260904-monza-wireless-v6-10-d8c5042b3efd@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Loic Poulain <loic.poulain@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Ricardo Salveti <ricardo.salveti@oss.qualcomm.com>

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260904-monza-wireless-v6-10-d8c5042b3efd@oss.qualcomm.com]
---
 .../bindings/connector/pcie-m2-e-connector.yaml           | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

